-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1097: a LEST that nothing can reach.
--
-- For MUST, DO and MAY the LEST is what follows when the deadline passes, so
-- a rule with no deadline (no WITHIN, no BEFORE, and under EVERY no WITHIN on
-- its ONCE or UPON EACH line) never reaches its LEST, and `l4 check` warns
-- at the LEST. MUST NOT is the exception: its LEST follows the forbidden act,
-- deadline or not. Each rule is traced with a long wait (or, for MUST NOT,
-- the forbidden act), so the results below show the evaluator agreeing with
-- each warning, and with each absence of one.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord
    Tenant HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Act IS ONE OF payRent, refund, smoke

alice   MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
tenants MEANS LIST alice

§ `Warned: no deadline`

-- The issue's own case. A million days on, the rent is still owed and the
-- LEST has not followed.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`rent, no deadline` MEANS
    PARTY alice
    MUST  payRent
    LEST  PARTY Landlord MUST refund WITHIN 10

#TRACE `rent, no deadline` AT 0 WITH
  (WAITUNTIL 1000000)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`DO, no deadline` MEANS
    PARTY alice
    DO    payRent
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `DO, no deadline` AT 0 WITH
  (WAITUNTIL 1000000)

-- A MAY with no deadline never runs out, so its LEST never follows.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`MAY, no deadline` MEANS
    PARTY alice
    MAY   payRent
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `MAY, no deadline` AT 0 WITH
  (WAITUNTIL 1000000)

-- AFTER opens the window; nothing closes it.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`AFTER alone` MEANS
    PARTY alice
    MUST  payRent
    AFTER 10
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `AFTER alone` AT 0 WITH
  (WAITUNTIL 1000000)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`everyone, no deadline` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST  payRent
        ONCE  ALL HAVE
        LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `everyone, no deadline` AT 0 WITH
  (WAITUNTIL 1000000)

-- Only the rule under the LEST is warned: the outer rule has a deadline.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`nested, inner has none` MEANS
    PARTY  alice
    MUST   payRent
    WITHIN 30
    LEST
        PARTY alice
        MUST  refund
        LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `nested, inner has none` AT 0 WITH
  (WAITUNTIL 1000000)

§ `Not warned`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`rent within 30` MEANS
    PARTY  alice
    MUST   payRent
    WITHIN 30
    LEST   PARTY Landlord MUST refund WITHIN 10

#TRACE `rent within 30` AT 0 WITH
  (WAITUNTIL 1000000)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`rent before a date` MEANS
    PARTY  alice
    MUST   payRent
    BEFORE (YMD 2026 6 30)
    LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `rent before a date` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  (WAITUNTIL (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2027 1 1)))

-- The deadline is on the ONCE line, and it bounds each member's act too.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`everyone within 30` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST  payRent
        ONCE  ALL HAVE WITHIN 30
        LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `everyone within 30` AT 0 WITH
  (WAITUNTIL 1000000)

-- The forbidden act reaches the LEST with no deadline at all.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`no smoking` MEANS
    PARTY    alice
    MUST NOT smoke
    LEST     PARTY Landlord MUST refund WITHIN 10

#TRACE `no smoking` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES smoke AT 5

-- No LEST, nothing to warn about.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`rent, HENCE only` MEANS
    PARTY alice
    MUST  payRent
    HENCE FULFILLED

#TRACE `rent, HENCE only` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES payRent AT 3
